However, it would be more fun if there would be more serious 
spellcasting monsters.  OTOH, it seems to be a bit complicated 
to make them casting spells cleverly.  

> You make a really good point, though.  When your character has the usual 
> stats (MC3, -50AC, etc), you consider it a rare emergency when in one in 
> ten ascensions a cockatrice/slime/vampire/etc actually manages to get a 
> hit through both AC and magic cancellation.  We have a lot of deaths to 
> cockatrices, but they basically never happen due to their natural attacks.
> 
> 
> A proposed fix would be to have some special attacks that are _not_ 
> rendered harmless by magic cancellation, akin to the way Vlad ignores MC 
> in the vlad_balance patch.

My suggestions would involve more sinister attacks.  

My favourite would be luckdrain (luck is quite 
important in particular for combat wombats), 
which could be caused, say, by higher demon/vampire 
attacks (as a bonus, one could distinguish vampires 
and their lords other than 'needs two hits more to 
go down'), which would not be affected by MC.  
Multiple blessed luck items could grant some 
resistance probability.  Or not.  

The next idea is to have 'smashing' attacks for 
giantkin, which may destroy easily breakable objects 
(Your glass wand called WISHING is crushed by the 
ettin's smash!) in the main inventory; if a container 
is hit, some random objects inside break (The ettin 
hits your blessed bag of holding!  You hear something 
crush inside it!).  Would teach many an adventurer the 
proper respect for really grown-up people.  

Another idea would be to place a curse on players, 
which would be more annoying than threatening; over a 
random period of time, you have a chance each turn 
of losing one to four stat points, get sick (like 
with tripes or rotten eggs), confused or stunned.  

The disenchanter idea could be carried further as 
well; some monsters could steal charges from wands 
in the inventory and maybe even use them against you.  

Another pet idea is the widening of intrinsic theft, 
making powerful fire creatures capable of stealing the 
fire resistance, or ice devils the ice resistance.  

Last not least it is still not plausible to me why 
a cloak of magic resistance can survive indefinitely 
many fire traps and fireballs.  Of course, if one 
would introduce armor/weapon destruction by damage, one 
should also improve armor/weapon repair possibilities 
a little.  

Maybe one should not incorporate all of these ideas, 
or else only marvin could ascend in the next version.. 

